server/tests\gdx-7-apply-costs-on-roll.test.js-4- * Three layers, matching the story's own AC9:
server/tests\gdx-7-apply-costs-on-roll.test.js-5- *  1. `pools.js`'s `getPool()` field threading (AC1) — the new
server/tests\gdx-7-apply-costs-on-roll.test.js:6: *     `vitae_cost`/`willpower_cost` fields mirror the existing `cost` string
server/tests\gdx-7-apply-costs-on-roll.test.js-7- *     threading, with `0` (a confirmed-free power, gdx.6) staying distinct
server/tests\gdx-7-apply-costs-on-roll.test.js-8- *     from `null` (never migrated/unparsed).
server/tests\gdx-7-apply-costs-on-roll.test.js-9- *  2. `roll-v2.js`'s three pure decision functions (AC3, AC5, AC6) —
server/tests\gdx-7-apply-costs-on-roll.test.js-10- *     `spendableCost`, `canAffordCost`, `rollButtonLabel` — exported
server/tests\gdx-7-apply-costs-on-roll.test.js-11- *     specifically so the spend decision is testable without a browser.
